// The client binding: every fact the runtime reads out of the client, one row per fact.
//
// A row is realised three times from this one table:
//   - as a member of wxl_core_init (wxl/core/init.h): the accessor the recompiled client hands
//     over at WarcraftXLInit, in table order, appended and never reordered;
//   - as wxl::core::binding::<name>, the function the seam bodies and wxl.object call, which on
//     x64 forwards to that accessor (src/binding/BindingTable.cpp) and on x86 reads the client's
//     memory at an offset of layouts.def (src/binding/BindingX86.cpp);
//   - on the client's side, as the function the fork assigns to the accessor
//     (client/WarcraftXL/Binding.cpp), which the fork's own compiler checks against the member.
//
// Row shapes. `name` is the accessor's name on every side. `ret` is the C type answered.
// `absent` is what the function answers when the client handed no accessor (x64) or the
// executable is not the client (x86).
//
//   WXL_BINDING(name, ret, params, args, absent)
//       a fact read by a call: params is the parenthesised parameter list, args the same names
//       in parentheses, as the x64 forwarder passes them. The x86 body is written by hand in
//       BindingX86.cpp; a row without one fails to link.
//
//   WXL_BINDING_FIELD(name, ret, Type, member, absent)
//       ret name(const void* object): the member of the object, read at
//       WXL_FIELD(#Type, member) on x86. Type is the id of a layouts.def type, member its
//       designator as a string.
//
//   WXL_BINDING_FIELD_VIA(name, ret, Type, via, ViaType, member, absent)
//       ret name(const void* object): the object's `via` member is a pointer to a ViaType block
//       (a descriptor), and the fact is that block's `member`. Absent when the pointer is null.
//
//   WXL_BINDING_FIELD_VIA_INDEX(name, ret, Type, via, ViaType, member)
//       wxl_bool name(const void* object, uint32_t index, ret* out): element `index` of the
//       array `member` of ret, bounded by sizeof(member) as layouts.def measured it. False past
//       the bound; the value goes to *out.
//
//   WXL_BINDING_FIELD_VIA_AT(name, ret, Type, via, ViaType, member, Elem, elem_member)
//       the same for an array of Elem structs, reading each element's `elem_member`.
//
// A consumer defines WXL_BINDING and, when it realises field reads differently, the field
// shapes; the ones it leaves undefined collapse onto WXL_BINDING with the signatures above.
// One domain per file under binding/, in the order below; a new fact is one row there.
// Copyright (C) 2026 WarcraftXL
